<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Window background painted by Android between process start and Flutter's first
  frame — API 21+ variant.

  minSdk is 21 (see android/app/build.gradle.kts), so THIS file is the one every
  supported device actually resolves; the base drawable/launch_background.xml
  is kept only for tooling that expects a base drawable to exist and is not
  loaded on any device this app ships to.

  This was `?android:colorBackground`, a theme attribute that resolves to
  Theme.Light's background (a light color) in day mode via values/styles.xml,
  or Theme.Black's background (black) in night mode via
  values-night/styles.xml. In day mode that reintroduced the exact
  white-flash-on-cold-start regression the base file's comment describes as
  fixed: the earlier fix landed in a resource the OS never loads for this app.

  MUST match AppColors.bgBase (#000000), unconditionally in both day and
  night mode: this app has no light theme.

  If you ever add a brand mark here, add it as a second <item> with a bitmap
  and gravity="center", and mirror it in values-v31/styles.xml so Android 12+
  shows the same thing. Divergence between those two files is the usual cause
  of a double-splash.
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item android:drawable="@android:color/black" />
</layer-list>
